<file path="README.md">
# my-turborepo

A Turborepo monorepo combining:

- **apps/api** — NestJS, exposing a **tRPC** router at `/trpc` and using
  `@thallesp/nestjs-better-auth` to guard routes and issue sessions.
- **apps/web** — Next.js 16 (App Router), consuming the API through a
  type-safe **tRPC React Query** client and the **Better Auth** React client,
  styled with **shadcn/ui**.
- **packages/ui** — shared shadcn/ui components (`@rocky/ui`), installed and
  imported the same way in every workspace via the CLI's monorepo mode.
- **packages/api** — shared DTOs/types consumed by both apps.
- **packages/eslint-config**, **packages/typescript-config**,
  **packages/jest-config** — shared tooling presets.

## Why auth lives in the API

`better-auth` is instantiated once, in `apps/api/src/auth/auth.ts`. The
Next.js app never mounts its own `/api/auth/[...all]` route — instead
`apps/web/lib/auth-client.ts` points `createAuthClient` at
`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL`, and `credentials: "include"` keeps the session cookie
flowing cross-origin.

## tRPC via `nestjs-trpc-v2`

`apps/api` uses [`nestjs-trpc-v2`](https://www.nestjs-trpc-v2.io)'s
decorator-based adapter rather than wiring `initTRPC` by hand:

- **`trpc/app.context.ts`** implements `TRPCContext` and reads the Better
  Auth session on every request, exposing `{ req, res, session }` as `ctx`.
- **`trpc/middlewares/protected.middleware.ts`** implements `TRPCMiddleware`.
  If `ctx.session` is missing it throws `TRPCError({ code: 'UNAUTHORIZED' })`;
  otherwise it merges `auth: { userId }` into `ctx`, which becomes available,
  fully typed, as `ProtectedMiddlewareContext` (from `nestjs-trpc-v2/types`)
  in any procedure annotated `@UseMiddlewares(ProtectedMiddleware)`.
- **`trpc/middlewares/logging.middleware.ts`** is a second, composable
  middleware — router-level `@UseMiddlewares()` runs before procedure-level
  ones, so `UserRouter` logs every call and layers auth on top per-procedure.
- **`trpc/routers/user.router.ts`** shows a public `@Query`, a protected
  `@Query`, and a protected `@Mutation` that wraps errors in `TRPCError`.
- **`trpc/routers/notification.router.ts`** shows a `@Subscription` using
  the `EventEmitter` + `tracked()` pattern for auto-reconnecting real-time
  updates; `apps/web/lib/trpc.ts` splits subscription traffic to
  `httpSubscriptionLink` and everything else to `httpBatchLink`.
- **`app.module.ts`** registers everything via `TRPCModule.forRoot({
  autoSchemaFile: './src/@generated', context: AppContext })`. That module
  writes a schema file on every build, which the web app imports as a
  type-only `AppRouter` — no manual codegen step.

## Adding shadcn components

Because both `components.json` files (in `packages/ui` and `apps/web`) point
their `ui` alias at `@rocky/ui/components`, you can run the CLI from either
workspace and components land in the shared package automatically:

```bash
cd apps/web
npx shadcn@latest add card
```

## Adding a tRPC router

1. Create `apps/api/src/trpc/routers/<name>.router.ts`, decorate the class
   with `@Injectable()` and `@Router({ alias: '<name>' })`, and add
   `@Query()` / `@Mutation()` / `@Subscription()` methods (see
   `user.router.ts` and `notification.router.ts`).
2. Add it to the `providers` array in `app.module.ts` — `TRPCModule` picks
   it up automatically, no manual router-merging required.
3. Restart `apps/api` once so `autoSchemaFile` regenerates
   `src/@generated`; the new router then shows up on `trpc.<name>` in
   `apps/web/lib/trpc.ts` with full type safety.

## Getting started

```bash
pnpm install
cp .env.example .env
pnpm dev
```

- API: http://localhost:3000 (tRPC at `/trpc`, auth at `/api/auth/*` via
  Better Auth's own handler mounted inside Nest)
- Web: http://localhost:3001
</file>

